---
title: DOM Host
description: Mount, update, size, interact with, and destroy a TanStack Chart in a browser DOM container.
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountChart"},{"type":"text","value":" is the framework-neutral default SVG browser host. It owns\nresponsive measurement, scene updates, keyed SVG reconciliation, animation,\npointer and keyboard interaction, built-in DOM tooltips, font relayout, and cleanup."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { mountChart } from '@tanstack/charts/dom'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"signature","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signature"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function mountChart<\n  TDatum,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  container: HTMLElement,\n  initialOptions: ChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n  runtime?: ChartRuntime<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n): ChartHost<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The optional runtime is for adapters or advanced applications that already\nrendered an initial scene. Ownership transfers to the host: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"host.destroy()"},{"type":"text","value":"\nalso destroys that runtime. In ordinary vanilla use, omit it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-use","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic use"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const options = {\n  definition: defineChart(definition, { tooltip }),\n  height: 320,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n}\n\nconst host = mountChart(container, options)\n\nhost.update({\n  ...options,\n  height: 400,\n})\n\nhost.destroy()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Application changes use a new definition:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const host = mountChart(container, {\n  definition: createDefinition(rows, 'revenue'),\n  ariaLabel: 'Revenue by month',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The definition identity is the application update boundary. Responsive\ndefinitions still rebuild when their resolved surface size changes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"renderer-neutral-and-canvas-hosts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer-neutral and Canvas hosts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the lower-level host when the surface is not necessarily SVG:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { canvasChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/canvas'\nimport { mountChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/renderer'\n\nconst host = mountChartRenderer(container, {\n  definition: defineChart(definition, { tooltip }),\n  renderer: canvasChartRenderer,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererHostOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" and returns a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererHost"},{"type":"text","value":". Its host lifecycle matches "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountChart"},{"type":"text","value":", but "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderer"},{"type":"text","value":"\nis required and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRender"},{"type":"text","value":" receives a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRendererRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":" containing the live "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSurface"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the built-in Canvas renderer, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountCanvasChart"},{"type":"text","value":" from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/canvas"},{"type":"text","value":" removes the explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderer"},{"type":"text","value":" option and returns a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CanvasChartHost"},{"type":"text","value":". Both hosts preserve the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interaction"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getScene"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"destroy"},{"type":"text","value":" model."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"host-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Host options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default SVG host requires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"definition"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ariaLabel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"definition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart definition"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Its identity is the application update boundary."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ariaLabel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accessible chart name placed on the SVG."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ariaDescription"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional SVG description."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Container or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"320"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fixed scene height in CSS pixels. When absent, a valid aspect ratio, then positive container content height, owns it."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Computes height as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width / aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":" when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" is absent and the ratio is positive and finite."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Container content width"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fixed scene width. Supplying it disables width observation."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"640"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Width used when a responsive container has not produced a positive measurement."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extra class on the rendered chart surface, not the container."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Empty"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefix for renderer-owned resource IDs. Use a unique value for resource-aware charts."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tabIndex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG tab index while keyboard behavior is enabled."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFocusChange"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Receives the primary focused point or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFocusGroupChange"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Receives all points selected by the current focus strategy."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSelect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Receives the clicked or keyboard-activated point, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" for an empty click."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRender"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runs after reconciliation with the container, default SVG, complete surface, scene, and interaction controller."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderSvg"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChartSvg"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replaces the scene-to-SVG renderer."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureText"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DOM font measurer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replaces guide text measurement."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The definition owns these chart controls:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxFocusDistance"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"48"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maximum scene-pixel distance for default pointer focus"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focus"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nearest point"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pointer grouping and keyboard navigation strategy; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" disables chart-owned focus and its generated layer"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusRing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generated primary-point indicator; an options object styles it and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps authored focus layers only"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cursor"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus-snapped or free application-owned cursor binding"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spatialIndex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Linear nearest-point scan"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dense-data nearest-point index"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgAnimation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keyed attribute, enter, and exit animation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pointer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic pointer focus, leave, and click handling"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyboard"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keyboard focus and navigation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in DOM tooltip content, placement, layering, and pinning"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyboard: false"},{"type":"text","value":" takes precedence over host "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tabIndex"},{"type":"text","value":". A negative\ncustom tab index can keep chart keyboard behavior available for programmatic\nfocus without placing the chart in the normal tab order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction options are detailed in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./focus-and-interaction.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus and interaction"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Renderer and animation\noptions are detailed in "},{"type":"link","href":"./rendering-and-export.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering and export"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"responsive-sizing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive sizing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" is absent, the host reads the container's content-box width. When\nboth "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" and a valid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":" are absent, it also reads the\ncontent-box height. Padding and borders stay outside the scene. The host\nobserves either container-owned dimension with the container document's\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ResizeObserver"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"mountChart(container, {\n  definition,\n  aspectRatio: 16 / 9,\n  initialWidth: 720,\n  ariaLabel: 'Traffic over time',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The fallback order is:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"positive container content width"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"640"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Height is explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":", then a positive finite "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":", then a\npositive finite container content height, then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"320"},{"type":"text","value":". Explicit height and\naspect ratio remain authoritative when the container's CSS height changes. A\nfixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" disables width observation but does not disable height\nobservation when both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" and a valid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":" are absent. The host\nschedules responsive relayout on the document's animation frame and skips\nresponsive relayouts when neither live dimension changed. Zero and nonfinite\nmeasurements do not replace the current scene. Resize relayout commits\nimmediately by default; set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgAnimation.resize"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" to animate it.\nContainer-owned height must resolve independently of the chart surface, such\nas a fixed-height card, grid row, flex item, or remaining track. When the chart\nitself would size a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height: auto"},{"type":"text","value":" container, supply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":"\ninstead so the surface is not also its own resize input."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The host temporarily assigns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"position: relative"},{"type":"text","value":" when the container's\ncomputed position is static, because local DOM tooltips are absolutely\npositioned inside it. Adding the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"portal"},{"type":"text","value":" extension to the tooltip options\ninstead places the tooltip in the browser top layer through a manual Popover,\nor directly under the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ownerDocument"},{"type":"text","value":" body as a fixed fallback, and positions\nit against the viewport. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"destroy"},{"type":"text","value":" restores the previous inline position when\nthe host owned that change and removes its tooltip."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"font-measurement","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Font measurement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default DOM measurer inherits the container's computed font family, style,\nstretch, weight, direction, and letter spacing. Measurements are cached. The\nhost clears that cache and relayouts when:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the inherited font signature changes during "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the document font set emits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loadingdone"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureText"},{"type":"text","value":" to own the geometry or to make browser and nonbrowser output\nuse the same metrics. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./scales-guides-and-color.md#automatic-guide-layout","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scales, guides, and color"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor the function contract."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"charthost","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartHost"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ChartHost<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  readonly interaction: ChartInteractionController<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  update(options: ChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>): void\n  getScene(): ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  destroy(): void\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"interaction","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The stable interaction controller resolves client coordinates through the\ncurrent renderer presentation and can paint application-owned focus:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const position = host.interaction.clientToScene(event.clientX, event.clientY)\nconst target = host.interaction.resolvePointer(event.clientX, event.clientY)\nhost.interaction.setControlledFocus(target)\n\nhost.interaction.setControlledFocus(null)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A pointer resolution preserves pointer ownership across scene updates and\npresentation frames. A raw point uses programmatic ownership unless "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":"\nis supplied explicitly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use definition "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pointer: false"},{"type":"text","value":" when a long-press, drag mode, or another\napplication gesture decides when point inspection begins. Keyboard navigation\nremains enabled independently. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../guides/interactions-and-selections.md#controlled-point-inspection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interactions and Selections"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"update","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"},{"type":"text","value":" replaces the complete option set. Keep required options in every call.\nIt renders synchronously when definition identity, size, accessibility,\nrenderer, keyboard, ID, or text measurement changes. Interaction callbacks,\ntooltip formatting, focus strategy, animation settings, and the spatial index\ncan update without rebuilding the scene."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An interrupted animated render is canceled before the next reconciliation.\nWhen the focused observation can be restored after a scene rebuild, focus and\ngrouped focus are repainted against its new coordinates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getscene","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getScene"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the current compiled scene. It is useful for aligned application UI,\ndiagnostics, or custom interaction. Treat it as immutable."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"destroy","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"destroy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"destroy"},{"type":"text","value":" is idempotent. It disconnects resize and font listeners, cancels\nscheduled work and animation, removes interaction listeners, clears the\ncontainer, and releases an inline positioning change owned by the host. A\ndestroyed host ignores later updates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"browser-ownership","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser ownership"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The DOM host requires a live "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HTMLElement"},{"type":"text","value":" and its owning document. For static\nor server rendering, compile a scene and render SVG without mounting; see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./runtime-and-scene.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime and scene"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./rendering-and-export.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering and export"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"signature","text":"Signature","level":2},{"id":"basic-use","text":"Basic use","level":2},{"id":"renderer-neutral-and-canvas-hosts","text":"Renderer-neutral and Canvas hosts","level":2},{"id":"host-options","text":"Host options","level":2},{"id":"responsive-sizing","text":"Responsive sizing","level":2},{"id":"font-measurement","text":"Font measurement","level":2},{"id":"charthost","text":"ChartHost","level":2},{"id":"interaction","text":"interaction","level":3},{"id":"update","text":"update","level":3},{"id":"getscene","text":"getScene","level":3},{"id":"destroy","text":"destroy","level":3},{"id":"browser-ownership","text":"Browser ownership","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`mountChart` is the framework-neutral default SVG browser host. It owns\nresponsive measurement, scene updates, keyed SVG reconciliation, animation,\npointer and keyboard interaction, built-in DOM tooltips, font relayout, and cleanup.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { mountChart } from '@tanstack/charts/dom'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n```\n\n## Signature\n\n```ts\nfunction mountChart<\n  TDatum,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  container: HTMLElement,\n  initialOptions: ChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n  runtime?: ChartRuntime<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n): ChartHost<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n```\n\nThe optional runtime is for adapters or advanced applications that already\nrendered an initial scene. Ownership transfers to the host: `host.destroy()`\nalso destroys that runtime. In ordinary vanilla use, omit it.\n\n## Basic use\n\n```ts\nconst options = {\n  definition: defineChart(definition, { tooltip }),\n  height: 320,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n}\n\nconst host = mountChart(container, options)\n\nhost.update({\n  ...options,\n  height: 400,\n})\n\nhost.destroy()\n```\n\nApplication changes use a new definition:\n\n```ts\nconst host = mountChart(container, {\n  definition: createDefinition(rows, 'revenue'),\n  ariaLabel: 'Revenue by month',\n})\n```\n\nThe definition identity is the application update boundary. Responsive\ndefinitions still rebuild when their resolved surface size changes.\n\n## Renderer-neutral and Canvas hosts\n\nUse the lower-level host when the surface is not necessarily SVG:\n\n```ts\nimport { canvasChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/canvas'\nimport { mountChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/renderer'\n\nconst host = mountChartRenderer(container, {\n  definition: defineChart(definition, { tooltip }),\n  renderer: canvasChartRenderer,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n})\n```\n\n`mountChartRenderer` accepts `ChartRendererHostOptions` and returns a\n`ChartRendererHost`. Its host lifecycle matches `mountChart`, but `renderer`\nis required and `onRender` receives a\n`ChartRendererRenderContext` containing the live `ChartSurface`.\n\nFor the built-in Canvas renderer, `mountCanvasChart` from\n`@tanstack/charts/canvas` removes the explicit `renderer` option and returns a\n`CanvasChartHost`. Both hosts preserve the same `interaction`, `update`,\n`getScene`, and `destroy` model.\n\n## Host options\n\nThe default SVG host requires `definition` and `ariaLabel`.\n\n| Option               | Default                 | Meaning                                                                                                               |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `definition`         | Required                | [Chart definition](./chart-definitions.md). Its identity is the application update boundary.                          |\n| `ariaLabel`          | Required                | Accessible chart name placed on the SVG.                                                                              |\n| `ariaDescription`    | None                    | Optional SVG description.                                                                                             |\n| `height`             | Container or `320`      | Fixed scene height in CSS pixels. When absent, a valid aspect ratio, then positive container content height, owns it. |\n| `aspectRatio`        | None                    | Computes height as `width / aspectRatio` when `height` is absent and the ratio is positive and finite.                |\n| `width`              | Container content width | Fixed scene width. Supplying it disables width observation.                                                           |\n| `initialWidth`       | `640`                   | Width used when a responsive container has not produced a positive measurement.                                       |\n| `className`          | None                    | Extra class on the rendered chart surface, not the container.                                                         |\n| `idPrefix`           | Empty                   | Prefix for renderer-owned resource IDs. Use a unique value for resource-aware charts.                                 |\n| `tabIndex`           | `0`                     | SVG tab index while keyboard behavior is enabled.                                                                     |\n| `onFocusChange`      | None                    | Receives the primary focused point or `null`.                                                                         |\n| `onFocusGroupChange` | None                    | Receives all points selected by the current focus strategy.                                                           |\n| `onSelect`           | None                    | Receives the clicked or keyboard-activated point, or `null` for an empty click.                                       |\n| `onRender`           | None                    | Runs after reconciliation with the container, default SVG, complete surface, scene, and interaction controller.       |\n| `renderSvg`          | `renderChartSvg`        | Replaces the scene-to-SVG renderer.                                                                                   |\n| `measureText`        | DOM font measurer       | Replaces guide text measurement.                                                                                      |\n\nThe definition owns these chart controls:\n\n| Option             | Default                   | Meaning                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `maxFocusDistance` | `48`                      | Maximum scene-pixel distance for default pointer focus                                                        |\n| `focus`            | Nearest point             | Pointer grouping and keyboard navigation strategy; `false` disables chart-owned focus and its generated layer |\n| `focusRing`        | `true`                    | Generated primary-point indicator; an options object styles it and `false` keeps authored focus layers only   |\n| `cursor`           | None                      | Focus-snapped or free application-owned cursor binding                                                        |\n| `spatialIndex`     | Linear nearest-point scan | Dense-data nearest-point index                                                                                |\n| `svgAnimation`     | `false`                   | Keyed attribute, enter, and exit animation                                                                    |\n| `pointer`          | `true`                    | Automatic pointer focus, leave, and click handling                                                            |\n| `keyboard`         | `true`                    | Keyboard focus and navigation                                                                                 |\n| `tooltip`          | `false`                   | Built-in DOM tooltip content, placement, layering, and pinning                                                |\n\nDefinition `keyboard: false` takes precedence over host `tabIndex`. A negative\ncustom tab index can keep chart keyboard behavior available for programmatic\nfocus without placing the chart in the normal tab order.\n\nInteraction options are detailed in\n[Focus and interaction](./focus-and-interaction.md). Renderer and animation\noptions are detailed in [Rendering and export](./rendering-and-export.md).\n\n## Responsive sizing\n\nWhen `width` is absent, the host reads the container's content-box width. When\nboth `height` and a valid `aspectRatio` are absent, it also reads the\ncontent-box height. Padding and borders stay outside the scene. The host\nobserves either container-owned dimension with the container document's\n`ResizeObserver`.\n\n```ts\nmountChart(container, {\n  definition,\n  aspectRatio: 16 / 9,\n  initialWidth: 720,\n  ariaLabel: 'Traffic over time',\n})\n```\n\nThe fallback order is:\n\n1. explicit `width`\n2. positive container content width\n3. `initialWidth`\n4. `640`\n\nHeight is explicit `height`, then a positive finite `aspectRatio`, then a\npositive finite container content height, then `320`. Explicit height and\naspect ratio remain authoritative when the container's CSS height changes. A\nfixed `width` disables width observation but does not disable height\nobservation when both `height` and a valid `aspectRatio` are absent. The host\nschedules responsive relayout on the document's animation frame and skips\nresponsive relayouts when neither live dimension changed. Zero and nonfinite\nmeasurements do not replace the current scene. Resize relayout commits\nimmediately by default; set `svgAnimation.resize` to `true` to animate it.\nContainer-owned height must resolve independently of the chart surface, such\nas a fixed-height card, grid row, flex item, or remaining track. When the chart\nitself would size a `height: auto` container, supply `height` or `aspectRatio`\ninstead so the surface is not also its own resize input.\n\nThe host temporarily assigns `position: relative` when the container's\ncomputed position is static, because local DOM tooltips are absolutely\npositioned inside it. Adding the `portal` extension to the tooltip options\ninstead places the tooltip in the browser top layer through a manual Popover,\nor directly under the `ownerDocument` body as a fixed fallback, and positions\nit against the viewport. `destroy` restores the previous inline position when\nthe host owned that change and removes its tooltip.\n\n## Font measurement\n\nThe default DOM measurer inherits the container's computed font family, style,\nstretch, weight, direction, and letter spacing. Measurements are cached. The\nhost clears that cache and relayouts when:\n\n- the inherited font signature changes during `update`\n- the document font set emits `loadingdone`\n\nPass `measureText` to own the geometry or to make browser and nonbrowser output\nuse the same metrics. See\n[Scales, guides, and color](./scales-guides-and-color.md#automatic-guide-layout)\nfor the function contract.\n\n## `ChartHost`\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartHost<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  readonly interaction: ChartInteractionController<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  update(options: ChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>): void\n  getScene(): ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  destroy(): void\n}\n```\n\n### `interaction`\n\nThe stable interaction controller resolves client coordinates through the\ncurrent renderer presentation and can paint application-owned focus:\n\n```ts\nconst position = host.interaction.clientToScene(event.clientX, event.clientY)\nconst target = host.interaction.resolvePointer(event.clientX, event.clientY)\nhost.interaction.setControlledFocus(target)\n\nhost.interaction.setControlledFocus(null)\n```\n\nA pointer resolution preserves pointer ownership across scene updates and\npresentation frames. A raw point uses programmatic ownership unless `source`\nis supplied explicitly.\n\nUse definition `pointer: false` when a long-press, drag mode, or another\napplication gesture decides when point inspection begins. Keyboard navigation\nremains enabled independently. See\n[Interactions and Selections](../guides/interactions-and-selections.md#controlled-point-inspection).\n\n### `update`\n\n`update` replaces the complete option set. Keep required options in every call.\nIt renders synchronously when definition identity, size, accessibility,\nrenderer, keyboard, ID, or text measurement changes. Interaction callbacks,\ntooltip formatting, focus strategy, animation settings, and the spatial index\ncan update without rebuilding the scene.\n\nAn interrupted animated render is canceled before the next reconciliation.\nWhen the focused observation can be restored after a scene rebuild, focus and\ngrouped focus are repainted against its new coordinates.\n\n### `getScene`\n\nReturns the current compiled scene. It is useful for aligned application UI,\ndiagnostics, or custom interaction. Treat it as immutable.\n\n### `destroy`\n\n`destroy` is idempotent. It disconnects resize and font listeners, cancels\nscheduled work and animation, removes interaction listeners, clears the\ncontainer, and releases an inline positioning change owned by the host. A\ndestroyed host ignores later updates.\n\n## Browser ownership\n\nThe DOM host requires a live `HTMLElement` and its owning document. For static\nor server rendering, compile a scene and render SVG without mounting; see\n[Runtime and scene](./runtime-and-scene.md) and\n[Rendering and export](./rendering-and-export.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: DOM Host\ndescription: Mount, update, size, interact with, and destroy a TanStack Chart in a browser DOM container.\n---\n\n`mountChart` is the framework-neutral default SVG browser host. It owns\nresponsive measurement, scene updates, keyed SVG reconciliation, animation,\npointer and keyboard interaction, built-in DOM tooltips, font relayout, and cleanup.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { mountChart } from '@tanstack/charts/dom'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n```\n\n## Signature\n\n```ts\nfunction mountChart<\n  TDatum,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n>(\n  container: HTMLElement,\n  initialOptions: ChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n  runtime?: ChartRuntime<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>,\n): ChartHost<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n```\n\nThe optional runtime is for adapters or advanced applications that already\nrendered an initial scene. Ownership transfers to the host: `host.destroy()`\nalso destroys that runtime. In ordinary vanilla use, omit it.\n\n## Basic use\n\n```ts\nconst options = {\n  definition: defineChart(definition, { tooltip }),\n  height: 320,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n}\n\nconst host = mountChart(container, options)\n\nhost.update({\n  ...options,\n  height: 400,\n})\n\nhost.destroy()\n```\n\nApplication changes use a new definition:\n\n```ts\nconst host = mountChart(container, {\n  definition: createDefinition(rows, 'revenue'),\n  ariaLabel: 'Revenue by month',\n})\n```\n\nThe definition identity is the application update boundary. Responsive\ndefinitions still rebuild when their resolved surface size changes.\n\n## Renderer-neutral and Canvas hosts\n\nUse the lower-level host when the surface is not necessarily SVG:\n\n```ts\nimport { canvasChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/canvas'\nimport { mountChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/renderer'\n\nconst host = mountChartRenderer(container, {\n  definition: defineChart(definition, { tooltip }),\n  renderer: canvasChartRenderer,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly revenue',\n})\n```\n\n`mountChartRenderer` accepts `ChartRendererHostOptions` and returns a\n`ChartRendererHost`. Its host lifecycle matches `mountChart`, but `renderer`\nis required and `onRender` receives a\n`ChartRendererRenderContext` containing the live `ChartSurface`.\n\nFor the built-in Canvas renderer, `mountCanvasChart` from\n`@tanstack/charts/canvas` removes the explicit `renderer` option and returns a\n`CanvasChartHost`. Both hosts preserve the same `interaction`, `update`,\n`getScene`, and `destroy` model.\n\n## Host options\n\nThe default SVG host requires `definition` and `ariaLabel`.\n\n| Option               | Default                 | Meaning                                                                                                               |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `definition`         | Required                | [Chart definition](./chart-definitions.md). Its identity is the application update boundary.                          |\n| `ariaLabel`          | Required                | Accessible chart name placed on the SVG.                                                                              |\n| `ariaDescription`    | None                    | Optional SVG description.                                                                                             |\n| `height`             | Container or `320`      | Fixed scene height in CSS pixels. When absent, a valid aspect ratio, then positive container content height, owns it. |\n| `aspectRatio`        | None                    | Computes height as `width / aspectRatio` when `height` is absent and the ratio is positive and finite.                |\n| `width`              | Container content width | Fixed scene width. Supplying it disables width observation.                                                           |\n| `initialWidth`       | `640`                   | Width used when a responsive container has not produced a positive measurement.                                       |\n| `className`          | None                    | Extra class on the rendered chart surface, not the container.                                                         |\n| `idPrefix`           | Empty                   | Prefix for renderer-owned resource IDs. Use a unique value for resource-aware charts.                                 |\n| `tabIndex`           | `0`                     | SVG tab index while keyboard behavior is enabled.                                                                     |\n| `onFocusChange`      | None                    | Receives the primary focused point or `null`.                                                                         |\n| `onFocusGroupChange` | None                    | Receives all points selected by the current focus strategy.                                                           |\n| `onSelect`           | None                    | Receives the clicked or keyboard-activated point, or `null` for an empty click.                                       |\n| `onRender`           | None                    | Runs after reconciliation with the container, default SVG, complete surface, scene, and interaction controller.       |\n| `renderSvg`          | `renderChartSvg`        | Replaces the scene-to-SVG renderer.                                                                                   |\n| `measureText`        | DOM font measurer       | Replaces guide text measurement.                                                                                      |\n\nThe definition owns these chart controls:\n\n| Option             | Default                   | Meaning                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `maxFocusDistance` | `48`                      | Maximum scene-pixel distance for default pointer focus                                                        |\n| `focus`            | Nearest point             | Pointer grouping and keyboard navigation strategy; `false` disables chart-owned focus and its generated layer |\n| `focusRing`        | `true`                    | Generated primary-point indicator; an options object styles it and `false` keeps authored focus layers only   |\n| `cursor`           | None                      | Focus-snapped or free application-owned cursor binding                                                        |\n| `spatialIndex`     | Linear nearest-point scan | Dense-data nearest-point index                                                                                |\n| `svgAnimation`     | `false`                   | Keyed attribute, enter, and exit animation                                                                    |\n| `pointer`          | `true`                    | Automatic pointer focus, leave, and click handling                                                            |\n| `keyboard`         | `true`                    | Keyboard focus and navigation                                                                                 |\n| `tooltip`          | `false`                   | Built-in DOM tooltip content, placement, layering, and pinning                                                |\n\nDefinition `keyboard: false` takes precedence over host `tabIndex`. A negative\ncustom tab index can keep chart keyboard behavior available for programmatic\nfocus without placing the chart in the normal tab order.\n\nInteraction options are detailed in\n[Focus and interaction](./focus-and-interaction.md). Renderer and animation\noptions are detailed in [Rendering and export](./rendering-and-export.md).\n\n## Responsive sizing\n\nWhen `width` is absent, the host reads the container's content-box width. When\nboth `height` and a valid `aspectRatio` are absent, it also reads the\ncontent-box height. Padding and borders stay outside the scene. The host\nobserves either container-owned dimension with the container document's\n`ResizeObserver`.\n\n```ts\nmountChart(container, {\n  definition,\n  aspectRatio: 16 / 9,\n  initialWidth: 720,\n  ariaLabel: 'Traffic over time',\n})\n```\n\nThe fallback order is:\n\n1. explicit `width`\n2. positive container content width\n3. `initialWidth`\n4. `640`\n\nHeight is explicit `height`, then a positive finite `aspectRatio`, then a\npositive finite container content height, then `320`. Explicit height and\naspect ratio remain authoritative when the container's CSS height changes. A\nfixed `width` disables width observation but does not disable height\nobservation when both `height` and a valid `aspectRatio` are absent. The host\nschedules responsive relayout on the document's animation frame and skips\nresponsive relayouts when neither live dimension changed. Zero and nonfinite\nmeasurements do not replace the current scene. Resize relayout commits\nimmediately by default; set `svgAnimation.resize` to `true` to animate it.\nContainer-owned height must resolve independently of the chart surface, such\nas a fixed-height card, grid row, flex item, or remaining track. When the chart\nitself would size a `height: auto` container, supply `height` or `aspectRatio`\ninstead so the surface is not also its own resize input.\n\nThe host temporarily assigns `position: relative` when the container's\ncomputed position is static, because local DOM tooltips are absolutely\npositioned inside it. Adding the `portal` extension to the tooltip options\ninstead places the tooltip in the browser top layer through a manual Popover,\nor directly under the `ownerDocument` body as a fixed fallback, and positions\nit against the viewport. `destroy` restores the previous inline position when\nthe host owned that change and removes its tooltip.\n\n## Font measurement\n\nThe default DOM measurer inherits the container's computed font family, style,\nstretch, weight, direction, and letter spacing. Measurements are cached. The\nhost clears that cache and relayouts when:\n\n- the inherited font signature changes during `update`\n- the document font set emits `loadingdone`\n\nPass `measureText` to own the geometry or to make browser and nonbrowser output\nuse the same metrics. See\n[Scales, guides, and color](./scales-guides-and-color.md#automatic-guide-layout)\nfor the function contract.\n\n## `ChartHost`\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartHost<\n  TDatum = unknown,\n  TXValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n  TYValue extends ChartValue = ChartValue,\n> {\n  readonly interaction: ChartInteractionController<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  update(options: ChartHostOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>): void\n  getScene(): ChartScene<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  destroy(): void\n}\n```\n\n### `interaction`\n\nThe stable interaction controller resolves client coordinates through the\ncurrent renderer presentation and can paint application-owned focus:\n\n```ts\nconst position = host.interaction.clientToScene(event.clientX, event.clientY)\nconst target = host.interaction.resolvePointer(event.clientX, event.clientY)\nhost.interaction.setControlledFocus(target)\n\nhost.interaction.setControlledFocus(null)\n```\n\nA pointer resolution preserves pointer ownership across scene updates and\npresentation frames. A raw point uses programmatic ownership unless `source`\nis supplied explicitly.\n\nUse definition `pointer: false` when a long-press, drag mode, or another\napplication gesture decides when point inspection begins. Keyboard navigation\nremains enabled independently. See\n[Interactions and Selections](../guides/interactions-and-selections.md#controlled-point-inspection).\n\n### `update`\n\n`update` replaces the complete option set. Keep required options in every call.\nIt renders synchronously when definition identity, size, accessibility,\nrenderer, keyboard, ID, or text measurement changes. Interaction callbacks,\ntooltip formatting, focus strategy, animation settings, and the spatial index\ncan update without rebuilding the scene.\n\nAn interrupted animated render is canceled before the next reconciliation.\nWhen the focused observation can be restored after a scene rebuild, focus and\ngrouped focus are repainted against its new coordinates.\n\n### `getScene`\n\nReturns the current compiled scene. It is useful for aligned application UI,\ndiagnostics, or custom interaction. Treat it as immutable.\n\n### `destroy`\n\n`destroy` is idempotent. It disconnects resize and font listeners, cancels\nscheduled work and animation, removes interaction listeners, clears the\ncontainer, and releases an inline positioning change owned by the host. A\ndestroyed host ignores later updates.\n\n## Browser ownership\n\nThe DOM host requires a live `HTMLElement` and its owning document. For static\nor server rendering, compile a scene and render SVG without mounting; see\n[Runtime and scene](./runtime-and-scene.md) and\n[Rendering and export](./rendering-and-export.md).\n"}
